{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29908 - PROTEIN:6147",
  "verbalization": "Aspafilioside C is shown to interact with Caspase-5, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol, Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate, and (4S,4aR,5S,8aR,9aS)-4a,5,6,7,8,8a,9,9a-Octahydro-4-hydroxy-9a-methoxy-3,4a,5-trimethylnaphtho(2,3-b)furan-2(4H)-one. All these compounds are linked to the Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9 through their target relationships. This suggests that Aspafilioside C may exert its effects through a common mechanism involving Caspase-5, which is a key player in the signaling pathways that regulate cellular responses to various stimuli. The shared interaction with Caspase-5 and the subsequent targeting of SDR family member 9 implies that Aspafilioside C may act through a pathway that involves caspase activation and subsequent downstream effects on metabolic enzymes. The evidence supports a potential role for Aspafilioside C in modulating these pathways, possibly through the activation of Caspase-5 and the subsequent induction of SDR family member 9.",
